  "decision": "As KerML 8.2.4.1.1 states it: the CONJUGATES terminal followed by one OwnedConjugation. CONJUGATES is not a production. It is one of the special lexical terminals of KerML 8.2.2.7, `CONJUGATES = '~' | 'conjugates'`, which match either the symbol or the keyword, so the rule writes it out as that two-way choice. The Xtext fragment expands it the same way. Unlike SpecializationPart, which the same clause states just above, there is no comma-separated repetition: a type conjugates exactly one other type.",
